'''Illusory labyrinth''' is a forbidden [[Spells|spell]] that creates a labyrinthine area that loops infinitely, making it impossible to escape.

==Description==
The spell contains the same central sigil as the [[Scalewolf Curse]], with column and directional signs, the remaining signs and sigils all being unidentified. The spell creates a grand underground labyrinth within which even space is distorted, as if you walk too far you will show up right where you started.

==Usage==
The spell is responsible for the formation of the [[Draconic Labyrinth Arc|underground labyrinth]], which [[Iguin]] trapped all of [[Qifrey's Atelier|Qifrey's Apprentices]] inside of. The spell was guarded by a [[Dragon|dragon]], which the apprentices had to get past using the [[Serpent's Bed of Sand]] spell they created, after which they destroyed the spell and were extracted by [[Qifrey]] from the labyrinth just in time before it collapsed.

